  <layout>One page of text in one column of verse, with the running head at the top right and the page number at the top left. Below the poem: "I. I. B." on its own line, then "POCILLI" in capitals, right-aligned. A dagger mark stands at the lower left. No margin notes.</layout>
  <page_number>92</page_number>
  <running_head>VARIA POEMATA.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">
      <i>Et quos lacteolo pinguior vbere</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Vates Gallia nutriit.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Verum perpetua si Sapientia</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Facundo referat iura recondita</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Ore, &amp; si placidis coetibus indicat</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Qua coelum petitur via:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Illi mella fluunt aemula nectari,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Sacro digna sonat rite silentio,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Et qua vulgus amat, turbaque doctior</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Intentis bibit auribus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Sic mirata suum Gracia Nestorem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Olim densa humeris dulciloquum audiit:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Quum verba eximiis picta leporibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Cano pectore promeret.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Sic mirata frequens audiit Herculem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Prisci temporibus Gallia Celticum,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Aures quum domitas duceret aureis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Victrix lingua catenulis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Sic Musis niteas Beza fauentibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Semper conspicuo vertice clarior,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Et nomen meritis laudibus inclitum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Cunctis Gentibus inferas.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Maiorem invidia te petat invidus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Ceu Cygnum streperis vocibus anseres,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Et ceu quum rabidus Lunam ululatibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Noctiurnus canis impetit.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27" para="true">I. I. B.</l>
    <l n="28" para="true">POCILLI</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The dagger mark at the lower left is a printed symbol, not text; it is not transcribed. The long s is read as plain s throughout. Some words are slightly soft in the scan: "pitta" read as "picta", "Beza" as "Beza", "Noctiurnus" as printed. The poem starts mid-piece, so the first paragraph is marked as a continuation. No Greek or Hebrew on this page.</notes>
</page>
